From: Project SunUEFI
Subject: [PATCH] input: report contact size and reject palms

Apply after the observability, raw-capture, pen-owner, epoch-reset and
line-noise patches.

Each touch peak is measured over the 4-connected cells at or above the
touch threshold. The finger node reports ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR/MINOR and
ABS_MT_TOOL_TYPE. A contact area of PALM_AREA_CELLS sensor cells or more,
palm_area_num_level2 of the stock touch configuration, is MT_TOOL_PALM,
one contact per palm area, and stays a palm until lifted. Palms never
press BTN_TOUCH. Contacts still down when a pen frame arrives are lifted
as palms, so libinput cancels them instead of delivering a tap.

The position axes now carry 13 units/mm from the 239x163 mm panel mode,
which libinput uses to place its pen arbitration area.

